The term scumming is appplied in roguelike circles to activies which are
not universally considered cheating, but are at least probably against
the spirit of the game.

There's no particular animus in referring to the activity as 'scumming',
but the name is there to remind you that it isn't really the way the
game was meant to be played.

Other examples, at least in angband include "town scumming", killing off
innocent townmembers to build up cash to buy items in shops, especially
since the shops do not change if you don't leave the town; "level
scumming" which involves going up and down stairs waiting for a level
that the game declares interesting, and other activities.

Some people have very passionate feelings about other people not save
scumming, but they can be safely ignored.  Do what makes the game most
fun for you.
